  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway where 2-Amino-3-methoxybenzoic acid interacts with Tankyrase-2 through a series of intermediate targets. This compound is linked to VMRC-LCP, which is a target of both Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine and Cocosamide B. These latter molecules, in turn, target Tankyrase-2, indicating a possible regulatory mechanism involving multiple pathways. The evidence highlights a dependency on VMRC-LCP as a common node, suggesting that 2-Amino-3-methoxybenzoic acid may influence Tankyrase-2 through this intermediate. The integration of these pathways implies that the compound may modulate Tankyrase-2 activity via a complex network of targets, potentially affecting cellular processes involving gene regulation. The strength of the evidence is supported by the consistent presence of VMRC-LCP as a shared target across different molecules, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between 2-Amino-3-methoxybenzoic acid and Tankyrase-2.",
